    "prompt": "Write down the first thirty-two numbers in base 4.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1, 2, 3, 10, 11, 12, 13, 20,$\n\n$21, 22, 23, 30, 31, 32, 33, 100,$\n\n$101, 102, 103, 110, 111, 112, 113, 120,$\n\n$121, 122, 123, 130, 131, 132, 133, 200.$",
      "worked": "Use the digits $0,1,2,3$. After a digit reaches $3$, carry to the next place: $3$ is followed by $10$, $33$ by $100$, and $133$ by $200$.\n\nThe first thirty-two positive integers in base 4 are:\n\n$1, 2, 3, 10, 11, 12, 13, 20,$\n\n$21, 22, 23, 30, 31, 32, 33, 100,$\n\n$101, 102, 103, 110, 111, 112, 113, 120,$\n\n$121, 122, 123, 130, 131, 132, 133, 200.$",
